 ('ENT_SUF_BAKHTIAR_KAKI','PER_ISL_CLASSICAL','Chishti saint of Delhi (d. 1235), foremost disciple of Mu''in al-Din Chishti; his shrine at Mehrauli anchors the Delhi Chishti tradition.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_BABA_FARID','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Punjabi Chishti saint (d. 1265), ''Baba Farid''; his verses are included in the Sikh Guru Granth Sahib. Shrine at Pakpattan.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_NIZAM_AWLIYA','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Pre-eminent Chishti saint of Delhi (d. 1325), ''Mahbub-i Ilahi''; his dargah is a major South Asian pilgrimage centre.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_AMIR_KHUSROW','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Indo-Persian poet and musician (d. 1325), devoted disciple of Nizam al-Din Awliya and a father of the qawwali devotional song.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_NAQSHBAND','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Central Asian saint of Bukhara (d. 1389), eponym of the Naqshbandiyya, who emphasized silent remembrance and presence in the world.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_KHWAJA_AHRAR','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Naqshbandi master of Samarqand (d. 1490) who gave the order great political and economic weight under the Timurids.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_BADAWI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Saint of Tanta (d. 1276), eponym of the Badawiyya and one of the most popular saints of Egypt.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_DASUQI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Egyptian saint (d. 1296), eponym of the Dasuqiyya (Burhaniyya) and counted among the four great qutbs of Egyptian Sufism.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_NIMATULLAH','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Persian saint and poet (d. 1431), founder of the Ni''matullahi order; his shrine at Mahan is a major Iranian pilgrimage site.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_BEKTASH','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Anatolian saint (d. 1271) revered as the founder-patron of the Bektashiyya and of Alevi devotion.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_YUNUS_EMRE','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Turkish saint-poet (d. 1321), father of Turkish-language Sufi poetry whose hymns of divine love remain central to Anatolian devotion.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_HAFIZ','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Persian lyric poet (d. 1390), ''Lisan al-Ghayb'', whose ghazals fuse the imagery of love and wine with mystical longing; venerated and used for bibliomancy (fal).'),
 ('ENT_SUF_SHABISTARI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Persian Sufi poet (d. 1340) whose Gulshan-i Raz (Rose Garden of Mystery) is a classic verse summary of Ibn al-Arabi''s metaphysics.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_JILI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Yemeni-Iraqi mystic (d. c. 1424) whose al-Insan al-Kamil developed Ibn al-Arabi''s doctrine of the Perfect Man.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_SAFI_ARDABILI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Persian saint of Ardabil (d. 1334), eponym of the Safaviyya order from which the Safavid dynasty later arose.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_HAMADANI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Persian Kubrawi saint (d. 1385) credited with spreading Islam and Persianate culture in Kashmir; ''Shah-i Hamadan''.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_MANERI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Indian Sufi master of Bihar (d. 1381) of the Firdausiyya (a Suhrawardi branch), famed for his Maktubat (Hundred Letters) of spiritual counsel.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_LAL_DED','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Kashmiri mystic poet (d. c. 1392), ''Lalla'', whose vakhs voice a non-dual devotion bridging Shaiva and Sufi piety; revered by Hindus and Muslims alike.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_NURI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Kashmiri saint (d. c. 1440), ''Nund Rishi'', patron-founder of the Kashmiri Rishi order; venerated as Alamdar-i Kashmir.'),
 ('ENT_SUF_JAMI','PER_ISL_MEDIEVAL','Persian poet and Naqshbandi mystic (d. 1492), last of the great classical Persian poets; his Nafahat al-Uns is a major saints'' hagiography.');
